CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--no-malloc-may-fail --dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --unwindset callee.0:4 --unwinding-assertions
^\[callee.assigns.\d+\] line \d+ Check that g\[.*0\] is assignable: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Check that a is assignable
Check that b is assignable
Check that k is assignable
--
Locals of a callee that are declared inside, or assigned inside, a loop
without a contract used to be checked against the caller's loop write set,
because DFCC took the local set of the innermost (uncontracted) loop rather
than of the scope whose write set is actually used for checking.
